{"title":"Career Roadmap · Sports Officer","role":"Sports Officer","summary":"A Sports Officer manages and develops sports and physical-activity programs in universities, colleges, schools, sports institutions, government organizations, residential campuses, clubs and other educational or institutional settings.","facts":{"Current degree":"Other Teacher Education (D.El.Ed / B.El.Ed / B.P.Ed / ITEP / Integrated B.Sc-B.Ed / BA-B.Ed)","Course":"Physical Education (B.P.Ed)"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Sports Officer manages and develops sports and physical-activity programs in universities, colleges, schools, sports institutions, government organizations, residential campuses, clubs and other educational or institutional settings."},{"type":"p","text":"The role combines:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Sports administration"},{"text":"Physical education"},{"text":"Event and tournament management"},{"text":"Athlete development"},{"text":"Sports facility management"},{"text":"Coaching coordination"},{"text":"Fitness and wellness programs"},{"text":"Budget and procurement management"},{"text":"Sports documentation and reporting"},{"text":"Team and stakeholder coordination"},{"text":"Sports technology and analytics"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A Sports Officer is generally more focused on managing sports programs and facilities than on being a full-time coach for one particular sport."}]},{"heading":"Career Pathway","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"flow","items":["Class 12","B.P.Ed / Relevant Physical Education Qualification","Teaching / Coaching / Sports Internship","Sports Coordinator / PE Teacher / Sports Program Executive","Sports Officer","Senior Sports Officer / Assistant Director – Sports","Deputy Director – Sports","Director – Physical Education & Sports","University / Institutional Sports Leadership"]},{"type":"p","text":"Alternative pathways can include:"},{"type":"flo